##Tell us about your personal history. Who are you? Where do you come from? Feel free to include some interesting facts.

I am a graduate of Tshwane University of Technology (TUT) with a national Diploma in Information Technology, specializing in communication networks. I grew up in a village called Tshitavha in Limpopo, where I developed a passion for technology, problem-solving, and learning how things work. From a young age, I was curious about computers and how they connect people, which eventually led me to study IT.
During my studies, I completed a 12-month work-integrated learning program as an IT Technician at the University of Venda. This experience exposed me to troubleshooting, networking, system administration, and IT support. I enjoyed solving technical problems and helping users, but over time, I became more interested in web development. I love the idea of building websites and applications that people can use every day.
Apart from my studies, I have worked on a public WiFi project, where I tested outdoor access points for speed, coverage, and security. This hands-on experience helped me understand how networks function in real-world settings. Additionally, I have completed certifications in Network Support, System Administration, and COMPTIA A+ 1000 - Part 2, showing my commitment to continuous learning.
On a personal level, I am a dedicated and hardworking individual. I have a 3-year-old daughter who motivates me to build a successful career so I can provide a good future for her. In my free time, I enjoy watching funny videos to relax, learning new tech skills, and exploring coding projects.
My journey so far has taught me the importance of persistence, adaptability, and always being open to learning. I am excited to develop my web development skills further and build a career where I can create innovative and useful websites that make an impact.

